Interpretation:
  1. Residues and q-coverage are necessary filters, not structure.
     Their fibers still mix rows with visibly different M and L.
  2. Additive relations and height-1 anti-coset counts improve the picture,
     especially around AP/Goddyn-Wong families, but still do not determine
     the exact obstruction.
  3. Topology-only safe-component data helps, but exact safe geometry
     (lengths plus boundary owners) is where the structure becomes almost
     determined.  This is solution-facing, but less so than exact M: it
     records which speeds carve the witness reservoir.
  4. Binding denominator data nearly determines M, but it is even more
     solution-facing:
     it is best viewed as a readout, not a proof input.
  5. The recurring determinant is not one scalar invariant.  It is a stack:
       CRT obligation -> additive anti-coset -> safe-component owners ->
       binding denominator.
     The hard rows are exactly where a lower layer looks ambiguous and the
     next layer resolves the ambiguity.
